[
  {
    "id": "sitl41-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 41 Mode names",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Flight-mode names end-to-end: request AVAILABLE_MODES (message 435 — in the bundled seed, absent from older common.xml revisions) on ArduPilot sysid 1 and PX4 sysid 11, then set a mode BY NAME on each (msg.payload.mode) and watch mode-changed records carry fromName/toName. AVAILABLE_MODES support varies by firmware version (Copter-4.7.0 and PX4 1.18 both answer; older AP may not) — a mute stack still resolves via the shipped tables, which is the ladder working, not a failure.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl41-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl41-tab",
    "name": "Mode names end-to-end",
    "info": "AP chain: request AVAILABLE_MODES with param2=0 — Copter-4.7.0 answers ONE frame of number_modes (measured 2026-08-18) — then a function node reads number_modes from that reply and emits the remaining per-index requests. PX4 bursts its full list from the single param2=0 request. Both requests prove the ACK; the walk itself rides delivery=send.\n\nSet mode by name: msg.payload.mode = 'GUIDED' on AP resolves through the vehicle-published cache (or the dialect's COPTER_MODE table before the cache fills); 'Position' on PX4 resolves into the decomposed main/sub pair PX4's DO_SET_MODE wants (DESIGN.md §14). The state feeds subscribe mode-changed only: each record keeps the raw from/to numbers and adds fromName/toName when the ladder resolves them.\n\nConnections: AP bind 0.0.0.0:14550 → 127.0.0.1:14551 (sysid 1); PX4 bind 0.0.0.0:14560 → 127.0.0.1:14561 (sysid 11).",
    "x": 220,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
